Wv"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nMax Weber famously wrote that politics is \"a strong and slow boring of hard boards.\" In [Why it took 4 years to get a lock files specification](https://snarky.ca/why-it-took-4-years-to-get-a-lock-files-specification/), Brett Cannon demonstrates how the same principle applies to technical coordination in open source.\n\nPython recently adopted [PEP 751](https://peps.python.org/pep-0751/) for lockfile specification. Doing so","key":"OtxyVb3IiB"}],"key":"YMtrONUwBL"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"X4FpE6MGBi"}],"key":"MdPfmx5wgm"},{"type":"text","value":"October 21, 2025 | ","key":"qY2SAv7rNj"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"j7D0jdLx2p"}],"key":"KlOWy85zMs"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"Ml1SpfuXuj"}],"key":"Sz9YByZqis"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/lock-files","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.lock-files.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"jEFvSfIg0M"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"My system for beating jet lag","key":"DiGda3Gvi3"}],"key":"H1eD2qEAlw"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nI travel internationally a lot, which means I deal with a lot of jet lag. This post is a quick summary of a system I've found helpful, based on [this paper](https://www.frontiersin.org/articles/10.3389/fphys.2019.00927/full).\n\n\nThe basic idea is to shift your body's internal clock by timing your exposure to light, exercise, and melatonin around","key":"XL9UKlFzGT"}],"key":"VGc36pKbAR"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"rRTIESL67K"}],"key":"WQdnWaazgw"},{"type":"text","value":"October 18, 2025 | ","key":"shkWaz600B"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"SNsfdaYCQx"}],"key":"QcYpYlDAti"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"cQEUYCEzXO"}],"key":"Xw9VoXT5Eg"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jet-lag","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jet-lag.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"dXd9BLyhkf"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why open source foundations try to fund systems, not development","key":"rEyjGwZjoF"}],"key":"Q8IlVfvKYD"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\nThis is a brief reflection on something that I've been hearing consistently from the Linux Foundation and its member projects as part of serving on the [Board of the Jupyter Foundation](https://jupyterfoundation.org). Here's a point that originally surprised me when I heard it:\n\n> Most foundations within the Linux Foundation network recommend","key":"BKKAiy7Z2X"}],"key":"KCH5xUIoDA"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"bPB4Ac6Zwf"}],"key":"rbFyG0jF5I"},{"type":"text","value":"May 31, 2025 | ","key":"CclL1b80zz"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"xqn98y3eYV"}],"key":"auM70RtxI1"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"smqyK98tiP"}],"key":"Eqdy9Meon5"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/fund-systems-not-developmend","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.fund-systems-not-developmend.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"NWos1nAKoi"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Jupyter can align the needs of its community and its foundation by enabling contribution","key":"wzqS69NEde"}],"key":"LzQrX8mzp3"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThis week was my first time attending the [Linux Foundation Member Summit](https://events.linuxfoundation.org/lf-member-summit/). This is an annual meeting for all of the Linux Foundation member organizations and projects. I joined because of my new role [on the Jupyter Executive Council](./jec.md), and so I tried to go into this meeting with the","key":"SxEfcEK5gF"}],"key":"o7PhHUMGNv"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"pqqEm2WFcq"}],"key":"sp6cuaPhaP"},{"type":"text","value":"March 22, 2025 | ","key":"s0xqFWIZDX"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"QkzGkkd9KN"}],"key":"D3bKqj6PWM"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"lj6bhbL7B5"}],"key":"QRfZhIkQyW"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/more-contributors","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.more-contributors.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"YDqR6L5rz4"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The relationship between the Jupyter Executive Council, Software Steering Council, and Foundation","key":"t9GO8z3lf1"}],"key":"QB6b5Javth"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis is a question that I've been asked many times now that I'm serving on the ","key":"BLaVbiCK01"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"Jupyter Executive Council","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JEC","key":"NjhYbacTK0"}],"key":"FG6TdJo7Sv"},{"type":"text","value":" and the ","key":"vzq3ZgyGhE"},{"type":"abbreviation","title":"The Jupyter Foundation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JF","key":"LR3oUEAuwe"}],"key":"kGhmJUgF1b"},{"type":"text","value":". I'm writing up a quick response so that I have something to refer back to and align my own thinking on.\n\n**How most Linux Foundation projects seem to be structured**. Linux","key":"z0gbgpXdpT"}],"key":"mjOEAzEwoR"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"cyommfI519"}],"key":"FOmUJd4z0Z"},{"type":"text","value":"March 02, 2025 | ","key":"oJfizyM1Xl"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"cLBmjv1Z6s"}],"key":"DYWpxioWTt"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"HDyZdCGIfY"}],"key":"N1QxfhTIoB"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/jupyter-org-structure","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.jupyter-org-structure.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"WiQzw2YhUC"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/os-support","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ways the Jupyter Foundation could support open source projects","key":"Mv2Ox9OHml"}],"key":"gOZlcy45BZ"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\nThe Jupyter Foundation has a pot of money and it aims to use that funding quickly to support the Jupyter Project. But what should it use the funding _for_? There are many things to do, and not enough time or money to try everything. This is a brief brainstorm and","key":"TOU9IcAwPM"}],"key":"OESLwbgu92"},{"type":"footer","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Date: ","key":"NpwriC1PNP"}],"key":"S7MzjIvOTg"},{"type":"text","value":"February 26, 2025 | ","key":"KAWgibOHnp"},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Author: ","key":"zMVP1BI2xf"}],"key":"HbqdRrhXKW"},{"type":"text","value":"Chris Holdgraf","key":"sO0X9FnDi6"}],"key":"YdwYsW2tRZ"}],"urlSource":"/blog/2025/os-support","dataUrl":"/blog.2025.os-support.json","internal":true,"protocol":"file","key":"YMQ7KvbcyA"},{"type":"card","url":"/blog/2025/jec","children":[{"type":"cardTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Why I'm running for the Jupyter Executive Council","key":"odA0GO3NQc"}],"key":"dHnp3QGQpy"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"\n\n\nThis year, I decided to nominate myself for the [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html). This is a brief post explaining my rationale for doing so, the kind of service I'd hope to provide the project, and where I imagine the project moving.\n\n\nThe [Jupyter Executive Council](https://jupyter.org/governance/executive_council.html) is the highest governing body within the","key":"NLnueXYPyA"}],"key":"xanXXShpT3"},{"type":"f